course: dictionary
lesson: 824
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning, so use the words around it to choose the right one. Belle can mean a very beautiful girl, a French word, or a girl's name. «She was the belle of the ball, and everyone wanted to dance with her.» The clues are ball and dancing, so a belle here is a very beautiful, admired girl or woman.
explain: In French, belle is the feminine form of beau, which means beautiful. Read «une belle maison» (a beautiful house). Maison is a feminine noun, so the adjective changes from beau to belle. Check the noun: if it is feminine, you will usually see belle.
explain: Belle is also a girl's name, like the heroine of «Beauty and the Beast». A capital letter is a clue that a word is a name. Ask yourself which meaning fits the sentence, then check that your choice still makes sense when you put it back in.
fact: A belle is a very beautiful girl or woman.
fact: «The belle of the ball» means the most admired girl or woman at a party.
fact: In French, «belle» is the feminine form of «beau», meaning beautiful, as in «une belle maison».
fact: Some adjectives change a lot: beau and belle (beautiful), nouveau and nouvelle (new), vieux and vieille (old).
fact: Belle is also a girl's name, as in the heroine of «Beauty and the Beast».
exercise: «She was the belle of the ball, and everyone wanted to dance with her.» What is a belle here? | A large party dance | A kind of French bread | *A very beautiful, admired girl or woman | A loud bell that rings at midnight
exercise: In French, «une belle maison» means what? | Old house | Beautiful house | *A beautiful house, with belle meaning beautiful | New house
exercise: Ella says Belle is in Beauty and the Beast. Which use of belle is a name? | la belle rose | une belle maison | the belle of the ball | *Belle, the heroine of Beauty and the Beast
test: Why is «belle» used instead of «beau» in «une belle maison»? | Because it is a plural word | *Because the noun it describes, maison, is feminine | Because it is a girl's name | Because it means very old
test: Which phrase means the most admired girl at a party? | Beauty and the Beast | Une belle-mère | *The belle of the ball | A Southern belle
exam: Which sentence uses belle as the French feminine form of beau? | *«une belle maison» | «Belle» from Beauty and the Beast | «the belle of the ball» | «a Southern belle»
